{"title": "Model diversification and tax scenarios", "text": "Compare potential sale, staged sale, charitable gifting, exchange fund, hedging, or hold strategies as applicable. Estimate tax impact, cash flow effect, and portfolio concentration change for each reasonable option. Model tax-aware sale scenarios that could fund part of Lila Pebblefizz's college shortfall without an unnecessarily large concentrated-position reduction at one time.", "priority": "medium", "assigneeId": "efbe58d1-6bfd-54b3-a7f9-fd9c22046941", "dueDate": null},
{"title": "Prepare advisor recommendation summary", "text": "Summarize key risks, viable strategies, tradeoffs, implementation requirements, and open questions for advisor review before client presentation.", "priority": "medium", "assigneeId": "c832e307-ebbe-5183-8f19-b2ba284474d8", "dueDate": null}
], "text": "Assess the concentrated holding, document the risk profile, identify tax-aware diversification options, and prepare recommendations suitable for client review. Include the position size, cost basis status, account registration, liquidity needs, restrictions, and any employer or insider-trading considerations using placeholders where client-specific facts will be added. Nadia Pebblefizz's Silver Marmot Robotics position is about $286,000 in a taxable brokerage account at Velvet Acorn Custody, roughly 22% of investable assets, with an unrealized long-term gain of about $171,000, and she asked for tax-aware sale scenarios that could fund part of Lila's college shortfall.", "evidence": "The review identified a sizeable taxable holding in Nadia's employer stock, and Nadia asked for tax-aware sale scenarios that could fund part of Lila's college shortfall without creating an unnecessarily large concentrated-position reduction at one time. The agreed follow-up is to prepare the Silver Marmot Robotics stock concentration and tuition funding scenarios by 2025-03-05."},
{"title": "Tax Document Collection Starter", "templateId": "20de386e-ad1c-5f93-aa1f-a8da447fe4f7", "priority": null, "dueDate": "2025-02-19", "assigneeId": null, "subTasks": [], "text": "Coordinate with the CPA the needed document list for Nadia and Owen Pebblefizz's 2024 tax file, which is missing education-related statements for Lila Pebblefizz's dual-enrollment coursework and the record of Iris Pebblefizz's $8,000 college gift.", "evidence": "The household's 2024 tax file did not yet include the relevant education-related statements for Lila's dual-enrollment coursework or the record of Iris Pebblefizz's college gift, and Nadia asked the team to coordinate the needed document list with the CPA. The agreed follow-up is to coordinate that needed tax document list with the CPA by 2025-02-19."},
{"title": "Coordinate beneficiary update request", "templateId": "cfef4f79-282e-5bfc-be83-12b2766ed2d5", "priority": "medium", "dueDate": "2025-02-28", "assigneeId": "b7c65af5-ac5e-56ab-a355-a3f6b5b97185", "subTasks": [], "text": "Confirm the requested beneficiary update, obtain the correct custodian or carrier form, prepare instructions for completion, and track the request through confirmation. Use placeholders for account registration, beneficiary names, relationship details, percentage allocations, and required signatures. Nadia Pebblefizz asked that the successor-owner update process for the Velvet Acorn Custody 529 accounts for Lila and Jonah be coordinated, since the successor-owner fields were completed years ago and may no longer align with Sera Bramblequill, the successor fiduciary named in the current estate documents.", "evidence": "Nadia also said the 529 successor-owner information may no longer align with the fiduciary named in the current estate documents, and she asked that the update process for the education accounts be coordinated. The agreed follow-up is to address 529 successor-owner alignment by 2025-02-28."}
